WEBVTT

00:00:00.00 --> 00:00:06.16
In the Southern Song era, Jin troops pressed at the border. A young man named Xin Qiji resolved to stand up and resist the Jin.

00:00:06.16 --> 00:00:10.72
Jin cavalry swept south, and the people of the Central Plains lived in deep misery.

00:00:10.72 --> 00:00:14.16
He led a handful of brave men and burst into the enemy camp deep in the night.

00:00:14.16 --> 00:00:18.84
Amid the firelight they charged straight at the enemy's great tent, unstoppable.

00:00:18.84 --> 00:00:22.16
They captured the traitor Zhang Anguo and returned in triumph.

00:00:22.16 --> 00:00:27.52
Zhang Anguo had been a Song general, but he had defected to the Jin, and everyone hated him.

00:00:27.52 --> 00:00:31.00
The people cheered to welcome them, and the young hero's name spread far and wide.

00:00:31.00 --> 00:00:34.00
That year he was barely in his twenties, yet he had already won undying merit.

00:00:34.00 --> 00:00:38.52
In his later years, he wrote lyrics by lamplight, pouring out the passion in his heart.

00:00:38.52 --> 00:00:41.60
His lifelong ambition to resist the Jin was written into his lyrics.

00:00:41.60 --> 00:00:45.72
His lyrics are bold and powerful, inspiring generation after generation.

00:00:45.72 --> 00:00:49.32
The name of this poet-hero will live forever in people's hearts.
